   178	
   179	By the sixth bell the man from the broadsides had copied it into his notebook at the gate lodge, and was riding down the hill with it as fast as a hired horse would take him. Cael watched him go from the north wall. The two coats at the foot of the road watched him go too. It was the first time in a week that either of them had turned his head.
   180	
   181	---
   182	
   183	Bracken's boy brought the enrollee's copy up to the residence at the seventh bell, in a grey folder under the house's seal, and Cael took it to his window and laid it on the sill and opened it at the first page.
