    98	
    99	Nobody in the house had settled what to call her. The council had needed two sittings to head her line in the accounts. The porter's wall gave her a rank, which said what she could do on a floor and nothing at all about what she did on paper. Cael waited for her to say she was no such thing. She let it stand, and he thought he knew why. It was the first title anybody had ever given her for the work, and not for the room she did it in.
