   112	
   113	Nine. And every one of them, Cael realized, was already somewhere in the right-hand column of Seln's sheaf. Not one was a witness, and not one was a finding about anything that had happened in a room. There was nothing on the leaf a person could be asked a question about, or caught out in, or shown to have misremembered. They were texts, the registry's own furniture, and a man did not bring furniture to prove a thing; he brought it to read aloud from, at the moment of his choosing.
