   191	Cael told him. Middle height and middle years. The brown coat, the cuffs mended in a different brown, the spectacles on their black cord, the inkwell with its screw lid. The way he had weighed the house's list in his palm before he opened it.
   192	
   193	Bracken listened with his hands flat on the counter. Then he went to the locked press, and came back with three thin bound books, and laid them side by side: the rolls of procurators admitted to practise before the registry seats of this district and the two beside it, each name with its date and its sponsor and, against some of them, a little ink drawing in the margin by some long-dead clerk with time on his hands.
   194	
