+# Book 6 whole-arc read — running notes
+
+Reader: Codex (fresh-context simulated cold read), 2026-10-11. These are working notes for Step 2, not manuscript edits.
+
+## Controls loaded before reading
+
+- Book 5 model read in full; report will follow its verdict + sections 1–10 structure.
+- Binding finish calendar: panel/ruling d201; council and last bout d202; M9 entry d203; academic year close d207; Line afterward. Shelf is the second camp past the Line and the first fire.
+- Season-blind. No season names, month order, or English weekdays. Halcenvane First-day through Seventh-day only.
+- Count locks: two renewals on paper except protected first pole in ch7/ch60 (“a stamp renewed four times”); lane bills ten / ten / twelve; Anchor perception about 10 / 12 / 14 feet; nine confirmed plus the uncounted anomaly; clean door d75→d115; Seln’s “twice more” remains two; Hesk’s clock loses time.
+- Offices: Gault = evaluator of record; the Archmarshal’s office = certifying office; challenge address = Caelen Hesk-ward.
+- Knowledge: Seln learns mechanism and reason for Shadow’s seal only in M6; seal holds while its use can be seen by anyone who could carry the seeing west. Kindling = the person’s Arbiter wakes and the brass plate lights; keeper’s frame reading/margin are the source record; corrections alter the registry entry and fail safe for Cael.
+- Reserved-text and owner-pending placeholders are not findings. No change may touch a protected run.
+- Entry seam read: Book 5 closes with seven confirmed plus the uncounted anomaly, two renewals on paper, Hesk’s clock restored to losing time, Brom’s review inside ninety days, Seln at the table, older watchers, and Vastin’s warning. Book 6 should open about two months later.
+- Exit control read: Book 7’s file still contains stale first-camp / “left in form” / Karis-ranking shorthand, but OWNER #46 and the B6 ledger govern; judge the manuscript against the ruling, not the stale plan text.
+
+## Running manuscript notes
+
+### Movement 1 — chapters 1–7
+
+- Entry seam holds. Ch1:5 opens “two months” after Book 5’s ferry; ch1:7 restores Hesk’s clock to losing time; ch1:29 carries two watchers at the landing and two at the road foot; ch1:33 has seven confirmed, Shadow sealed, and the still place uncounted.
+- Strong opening argument: the settled Storm is not a victory lap but makes the concealed band freshly costly (ch1:119–127); Ephram’s chart then turns the same fact into a relationship and a future promise (ch3:203–243).
+- The book teaches its legal weapon cleanly: service and the exact challenged name (ch5:65–73), integrity as a rule for a bad instrument (ch7:13–29), chapter fourteen’s human consequence (ch7:55–81), the corridor (ch7:121–129), then the first pole (ch7:225–227). A thirteen-year-old can follow the chain because each abstraction gets a person, object or door.
+- Count locks so far: non-protected record says renewals without inflating them (ch6:69); protected first pole alone says “renewed four times” (ch7:225). Lane bill introduced at ten counts, clean at eleven (ch4:191–215). Shadow’s rent and seal remain private to Cael/Lira/Brom/Karis; Seln is explicitly ignorant (ch4:237–245).
+- Gault is evaluator of record on Cael’s sheet (ch2:145) and acts as such in wing three (ch3:83–199). Challenge uses Caelen Hesk-ward (ch5:65).
+- Reader pull caught at ch1:109–129 (the flag clears without a notice) and again at ch5:53–79 (service). The honest-floor chapter earns its length: every capability supplies a rule needed later, and Brom’s “once a week” (ch4:247–269) makes concealment relational rather than merely tactical.
+- First texture watch: door/gate/frame/corridor language is already extremely dense across all seven chapters; much is thematic and protected, but the non-load-bearing similes may become audible book-wide. Also watch “for a while / long moment / nobody said anything,” square/flat gestures, and clauses glossing a gesture as characteristic.
+- No continuity defect found in M1 on the straight read. Possible audit-only item for later: ch1:51’s “four years trying to make [the landing beat] shorter” repeats Book 5’s protected close and does not explicitly date from Kindling; do not flag absent a contradictory ruling.
+
+### Movement 2 — chapters 8–13
+
+- Calendar progression is legible and so far exact: ch10:15 fixes the first sitting on the sixth Fifth-day; ch12:3 puts Lira’s rated trial on day 30; ch12:237 gives the advancement docket on day 31; ch13:91 puts the sitting on day 40. The numeric Fifth-day convention is compliant with the season-blind rule.
+- Lane bill ratifies cleanly in ch11:153–195: Lira ten, Force ten, Blade twelve; clean lines eleven, eleven, thirteen. The explanation lands as a bill rather than a banner or flag.
+- The first sitting earns its procedural length. Karis gives the reader the map before the room (ch13:69–87), then the hood and hands enact the thesis (ch13:129–139), Havel tests it from inside the office (ch13:143–185), and the coach names the consequence (ch13:207–217). This is the first full turn from “work within the system” toward “the system is the hand.”
+- Kindling boundary still holds on the straight read. Cael publicly remembers the pale circle, Pellin’s brass plate and its eleven-second delay (ch9:147; ch13:117–121), but neither narration nor Seln receives the Arbiter/corrections mechanism. Seln’s office knowledge remains institutional, not causal (ch13:215–225).
+- The Velmere letter is introduced as sealed on Brom’s table (ch12:255–267), then opened on the third evening (ch12:269–275). This appears to be a different, later letter than the binding day-45 envelope that must stay sealed; audit identity carefully when day 45 arrives.
+- Counts/roles hold: ch8:137–159 describes grant plus two renewals; ch10:113–119 and ch13:111–119 use Caelen Hesk-ward; ch11:153–195 has the 10/10/12 bill. Gault remains evaluator of record; no office-title drift noticed.
+- Lira’s rated bout (ch12:27–179) is long but functional: each exchange teaches settle/countermeasure, and the fourth/fifth burst converts a win into the precise control deficit. The injury consequence prevents spectacle from cancelling the bill.
+- Reader Standard holds. Legal abstractions are repeatedly converted to a physical map, table, seal, receipt or door. The one likely reread point is the distinction between a seat’s own-motion power and party motion (ch13:29–47), but Karis’s teaching scene resolves it in place.
+- Texture watch strengthened: “squared / square,” fingers beside lines, exact stillness, “for a long moment,” and silence translated into meaning recur frequently. Keep counting rather than treating thematic uses as defects.
+- No cross-movement continuity defect found in M2 on the straight read.
+
+### Movement 3 — chapters 14–20
+
+- The system-hand argument turns rather than merely repeats. Vastin discovers his own true assessment cannot enter the proceeding (ch14:98–120, 132–148); the house discovers the refusal travels as gossip faster than as notice (ch15:87–117); then Gault, Umber and Withrow each leave a constrained honest sentence in the official record (ch17:159–165, 191–211, 223–241). The book now distinguishes honest people inside an institution from the institution’s arranged effect.
+- The day-45 Velmere envelope is correctly identified and remains sealed: it arrives fourteen days after the day-31 letter (ch16:103–109), is still whole four days later (ch19:71), and sits sealed in Brom’s left pocket at the third sitting (ch20:127). The earlier letter opened in ch12 is therefore not the locked envelope.
+- Seln’s knowledge boundary holds. He can name a pre-restriction inventory / “walking the fences” from his office career (ch19:107–137), but he is still being allowed to teach Cael through records rather than being told about Shadow (ch18:161–217). Nothing gives him the concealment mechanism or reason yet.
+- Calendar/accounting holds: Archmarshal refused on day 44 (ch14:106–118; ch20:123–125); Daeva’s statement is day 54 (ch20:123–125); the five-office inventory is six weeks into a projected nine (ch19:121–137). Third sitting preserves the exact Caelen Hesk-ward log (ch20:127).
+- The third sitting is the movement’s necessary long scene. Karis/counsel pre-map the four-part argument (ch20:81–101); Jent concedes execution, provision and record (ch20:131–157); the counsel moves names→preamble→shelf→text (ch20:165–189); the ruling then holds every paper point while allowing re-evaluation to proceed (ch20:193–213). Lira’s bout analogy at ch20:217–231 passes the Reader Standard check in one pass.
+- The observer pressure accumulates coherently across movements: scouts first appear on Lira’s gallery (ch15:21–27), requests become a count and second ledger (ch16:37–67), four officers enter wing three (ch17:3–115), and Rooke closes Lira’s gallery because it has become a route to Cael (ch17:119–185). The cost lands on Lira rather than being abstract.
+- Count locks hold: the honest-floor lane bill remains ten counts (ch20:43–55, 69); Gault remains the person naming provision touches/figure and writing the minute (ch17:31–107, 159–165); two renewals on paper is explicit at ch16:123–135 and ch20:169–173.
+- Reader/rhythm watch: ch14 is a single-POV interior chapter and notably slower than the surrounding ensemble chapters, but each return to trays, the press, or the frame changes Vastin’s position; it earns the pause. Ch17 and ch20 are very long multi-scene chapters, yet both contain the movement’s principal fight/procedure turns. Verify as statistical outliers later.
+- Repetition watch: “squared to the edge,” quarter-turning cups/rules, a hand held over a pocket, “for a long moment,” and people saying nothing after a meaningful object is placed continue to recur. Several are character-specific motifs (Seln’s cup, Brom’s pocket) and should be protected from indiscriminate cleanup.
+- No cross-movement continuity or premature-reserved-truth defect found in M3 on the straight read.
+
+### Movement 4 — chapters 21–27
+
+- The road/Line alternative grows from independent facts rather than a sudden plan: Lira gathers three carters’ accounts separately (ch21:15–91), brings the 4/3/stamps/2/1 sum to the five-person council (ch21:169–257), and Brom’s governing answer is “Prepare both roads. Win the sittings. Keep a box” (ch22:41–51). Cael’s insistence on the text and Lira’s floor distinction keep the choice genuinely contested.
+- The Velmere day-45 envelope remains sealed and specifically twenty-three days unopened at the council (ch22:47–63). Its physical side stays consistent: Brom’s right hand goes to the left inside pocket.
+- Seln still does not know Shadow’s mechanism. His interior chapter gives his choice to file true-but-empty returns, his recognition that registry routes end where stamps end, and the kept material above the copying table (ch22:91–149). Those are his own office/monitoring facts, not the M6 disclosure.
+- The fuller confluence sequence earns its length. The setup establishes why a sealed meet line matters (ch23:41–59), the hall supplies four tactical facts (ch23:171–195; ch24:113–131), the bout converts craft into the one-point result (ch24:25–189), and the aftermath gives both the honest bill and the durable file line (ch24:193–233; ch25:119–139). The production order then contaminates Lira’s earned afternoon at the narratively exact moment (ch25:19–41, 47–77).
+- The fourth sitting advances the central argument cleanly: Karis gains the title “Advocate of record” in the door log (ch26:35–45); her one question forces Jent’s “None…discretion” into the minute (ch26:65–115); Cael understands that his receipts cannot answer a room not turning on evidence (ch26:101–113). No office-title drift: Gault explicitly remains evaluator of record (ch27:43–49).
+- Anchor introduction is appropriately incomplete. Cael observes position/lines but no action (ch27:61–83); Seln can name the rare service Path and its posting purpose but refuses to guess mechanics (ch27:105–129); the full-scale chalk reconstruction leaves reach/cost blank (ch27:153–195). Later audit must confirm the planned about-10/12/14-foot perception progression, which has not yet occurred.
+- Calendar locks visible here hold: the confluence meet is postponed eight days (ch21:93–97; ch23:171–173); default is corrected to forty days from the close of the fourth sitting, with absent then fled (ch21:223–255). No season/month-order/English-weekday language noticed.
+- Reader Standard holds in the tactical material because Cael promises to watch only Lira’s feet (ch23:105–123), then reports the bout in that channel. The procedural turn is distilled twice: receipts in a room that does not take them (ch26:101–113) and the schedule no longer theirs (ch27:213–223).
+- Rhythm watch: ch23–25 form a long meet suite. The bout itself earns the space, but the setup repeats several anticipatory explanations (sealed line/file/ladder) already established; on a same-author pass this is the first place where fullness may shade into re-briefing rather than new pressure. Ch26–27 then accelerate sharply into the riders/Anchor cliff.
+- Texture watch: “square to the edge,” exact measured times, object placement followed by collective silence, and a character looking “for a long time” remain the most audible general habits. The recurring floor→paper analogy is thematically necessary but may be over-explained in non-protected connective prose.
+- No cross-movement continuity defect or early reserved-truth spend found in M4 on the straight read.
+
+### Movement 5 — chapters 28–34
+
+- The paper/seal investigation builds cleanly from a sixteenth-inch watermark displacement (ch28:19–47) through the mended second run and unruled fourteenth lot (ch29:3–39), while Havel independently finds the seal absent from all three registers (ch30:13–87). These are convergent facts, not prematurely named reserved truth.
+- The road attack is the book’s decisive midpoint turn. The fourteen fixed points frame the cut and leave one controlled channel (ch30:189–205); the attackers arrive without paper, faces or blades and declare custody (ch30:213–239); four exchanges let Cael learn subtraction, predictive placement, accumulation and the moving first stitch (ch31:23–217); he acquires and reverses the system’s enforcement craft (ch31:219–259). The next sitting then demonstrates the thesis: the paper hand and road hand are the same body (ch32:258–268).
+- Fuller treatment earns its length here. The road action is long because every exchange supplies one component of the acquired fragment and one price paid by another person. The aftermath separately accounts Lira’s four bursts/right ankle, Brom’s left shoulder, Karis’s right hand/fourth ignition breach, Cael’s left forearm/right ribs, the horse and Seln’s unseen wagon work (ch32:50–122). That accounting is structural, not padding.
+- Anchor mechanics/counts so far: fourteen prepared points (ch30:195–205); four exchanges of observation (ch31:215–227); nineteen close cage points plus the moving stitch (ch31:191–203); fragment notice says contact-to-short range and Silver equivalent (ch32:25–40). The woman stands about fifteen feet away at the reversal (ch31:201), which is a scene distance, not yet the later 10/12/14-foot perception test. Audit those planned test distances when they appear.
+- Fragment count is correct at this stage: Anchor is the eighth confirmed (ch32:25–40; ch34:223–235), and the still place remains explicitly uncounted. The anomaly has not been promoted.
+- Knowledge boundary still holds through M5. Seln decides to open his case after recognizing the fourth grade / hand (ch29:43–103), but ch34 ends before the annex disclosure. He knows the service system and that Cael has concealed something from his returns; he has not yet learned Shadow’s mechanism or why it is sealed.
+- Velmere day-45 envelope remains sealed and physically intact after the road; Brom checks the left inside pocket (ch29:217–249; ch32:50–65).
+- Clean-door start appears to be the uncommanded twelve-second doorway at ch33:99–175, followed by naming/idle state (ch33:239–304; ch34:199–215). Verify against the ratified day-75→115 lock in the calendar audit.
+- Reader Standard holds through the complex Anchor fight because each abstraction is demonstrated physically before Cael names it. The one dense passage is ch31:191–227 (cage, moving stitch, lines through the fourteen), but the unthreading action immediately verifies the model.
+- Pacing: ch28–29 spend a long runway on paper provenance and Seln’s catechism, but both are required to make his case-opening choice credible. Ch33–34 give a deliberately full two-chapter recovery; the doorway accident, naming solution, cost curve, birthday room, three lost bouts and Hesk’s satchel all earn space individually, though the birthday chapter repeats the “good room / turned paper / nobody asks” emotional grammar at length.
+- **Calendar defect:** ch34:21 says “It’s the eleventh of Sowing.” This is a named month/date and contradicts the binding season-blind rule. Verify the intended numbered day (likely day 75) and protected boundaries before proposing the minimal replacement.
+- Texture watch: the book now has many scenes where a meaningful object is placed/squared, everyone is silent, and a final plain sentence interprets the silence. Also count “quietly,” “for a long time/moment,” “the way a man/person…,” quarter-turns, and “nobody said/asked.”
+
+### Movement 6 — chapters 35–40
+
+- The knowledge boundary lands exactly where required. Seln opens the case in M6 (ch35:153–191), the group reads station readings/orders, reports, memoranda and the advisory leaf before drawing conclusions (ch35:195–293; ch36:3–123), and Seln states the downward corrective practice once the paper supports it (ch36:127–173). Only after that does Cael disclose the fragments and Shadow’s origin/reason for sealing (ch37:1–208).
+- Shadow terms are exact and earned: Seln receives the whole story, including why his trade made public use traceable (ch37:119–178); the debt closes but Seln neither releases nor reclaims the fragment (ch37:188–202); his seal is “while its use can be seen by anyone who could carry the seeing west” and otherwise Cael’s without asking permission (ch37:198–208). The final inventory revision says “Sealed, on his terms” (ch37:250–268).
+- “Twice more” remains exactly two at ch37:97–107 and is repeated as two at ch37:258–262. No drift.
+- Kindling mechanics are finally and clearly paid out in the correct movement: the person’s Arbiter wakes and the station’s plate/reading apparatus records (Cael’s remembered Denvash at ch36:113–123); the advisory corrections function is appended to, not identical with, the reading (ch36:83–123); station keeper margins preserve reach before the entry order removes them (ch35:195–217; ch39:29–47); Cael’s eleven seconds are the function failing safe because there is no column / all margin (ch39:51–67). The distinction is followable on one read because the paper examples precede the theory.
+- The case respects reserved truth limits. Karis dates the policy to about two hundred years and establishes an older reading plus the former “Unbound” door (ch39:91–143), then explicitly enters as a limit everything below the case: what the reading is, who made it, how old it is. Session nine/anomaly remains untouched and uncounted (ch39:159–169).
+- Anchor perception locks are exact: sure/about ten feet, faint at twelve, nothing at fourteen (ch38:317–349). The trial distinguishes perception from reach and stops at the first near-fix, with Brom’s count remaining one (ch38:351–379). No fixing is normalized.
+- Clean-door calendar is explicit: fourth sitting closed day 75; absent becomes fled day 115 (ch38:165–203). This confirms the 75→115 lock. The annex disclosure is day 88 (ch37:250–262), and Greyvane leaves arrive day 91 (ch38:129–145).
+- Hesk’s clock still loses time (ch35:99–103). Gault remains evaluator of record in the earlier gate record and no later office drift appears. Velmere envelope remains sealed in Brom’s left pocket at ch36:127–139.
+- Arc turn fully pays: “the room was never the system” becomes “the honest people were in the drawer too” (ch35:271–291), then “it isn’t broken; it’s maintained” (ch39:191–219). Lira’s reframing of the cache as a map rather than evidence (ch39:229–253) converts revelation into the next movement’s action logic.
+- Vastin’s borrowed-room read earns its substantial length. Each of the four proposed risks is honored; he independently refuses verification, report and certification (ch40:201–219), refuses false alliance (ch40:221–247), and later lives the cost by leaving the northern girl’s file in observation rather than exposing her (ch40:251–329). His refusal to certify becomes a future causal lever, not consolation.
+- Reader Standard holds despite density because the narrative repeatedly distinguishes reading / function / entry with concrete paired sheets and explains why every available verification instrument is compromised. Nothing is unsuitable for thirteen.
+- Texture/padding watch: ch35–40 contain many variations of a bare/borrowed/good room, paper laid in rows, prolonged collective silence, hands flat on tables, and readers taking documents in order. Most carry character/epistemic meaning, but the cumulative ritual is audible; trim only non-protected connective repetitions, never the disclosure units.
+- Calendar defect from ch34 remains the only definite continuity failure through M6.

