+### Movement 6 — chapters 35–40
+
+- The knowledge boundary lands exactly where required. Seln opens the case in M6 (ch35:153–191), the group reads station readings/orders, reports, memoranda and the advisory leaf before drawing conclusions (ch35:195–293; ch36:3–123), and Seln states the downward corrective practice once the paper supports it (ch36:127–173). Only after that does Cael disclose the fragments and Shadow’s origin/reason for sealing (ch37:1–208).
