+- The observer pressure accumulates coherently across movements: scouts first appear on Lira’s gallery (ch15:21–27), requests become a count and second ledger (ch16:37–67), four officers enter wing three (ch17:3–115), and Rooke closes Lira’s gallery because it has become a route to Cael (ch17:119–185). The cost lands on Lira rather than being abstract.
