+# Book 6 whole-arc read — running notes
+
+Reader: Codex (fresh-context simulated cold read), 2026-10-11. These are working notes for Step 2, not manuscript edits.
+
+## Controls loaded before reading
+
+- Book 5 model read in full; report will follow its verdict + sections 1–10 structure.
+- Binding finish calendar: panel/ruling d201; council and last bout d202; M9 entry d203; academic year close d207; Line afterward. Shelf is the second camp past the Line and the first fire.
+- Season-blind. No season names, month order, or English weekdays. Halcenvane First-day through Seventh-day only.
+- Count locks: two renewals on paper except protected first pole in ch7/ch60 (“a stamp renewed four times”); lane bills ten / ten / twelve; Anchor perception about 10 / 12 / 14 feet; nine confirmed plus the uncounted anomaly; clean door d75→d115; Seln’s “twice more” remains two; Hesk’s clock loses time.
+- Offices: Gault = evaluator of record; the Archmarshal’s office = certifying office; challenge address = Caelen Hesk-ward.
+- Knowledge: Seln learns mechanism and reason for Shadow’s seal only in M6; seal holds while its use can be seen by anyone who could carry the seeing west. Kindling = the person’s Arbiter wakes and the brass plate lights; keeper’s frame reading/margin are the source record; corrections alter the registry entry and fail safe for Cael.
+- Reserved-text and owner-pending placeholders are not findings. No change may touch a protected run.
+- Entry seam read: Book 5 closes with seven confirmed plus the uncounted anomaly, two renewals on paper, Hesk’s clock restored to losing time, Brom’s review inside ninety days, Seln at the table, older watchers, and Vastin’s warning. Book 6 should open about two months later.
+- Exit control read: Book 7’s file still contains stale first-camp / “left in form” / Karis-ranking shorthand, but OWNER #46 and the B6 ledger govern; judge the manuscript against the ruling, not the stale plan text.
+
+## Running manuscript notes
+
+### Movement 1 — chapters 1–7
+
+- Entry seam holds. Ch1:5 opens “two months” after Book 5’s ferry; ch1:7 restores Hesk’s clock to losing time; ch1:29 carries two watchers at the landing and two at the road foot; ch1:33 has seven confirmed, Shadow sealed, and the still place uncounted.
+- Strong opening argument: the settled Storm is not a victory lap but makes the concealed band freshly costly (ch1:119–127); Ephram’s chart then turns the same fact into a relationship and a future promise (ch3:203–243).
+- The book teaches its legal weapon cleanly: service and the exact challenged name (ch5:65–73), integrity as a rule for a bad instrument (ch7:13–29), chapter fourteen’s human consequence (ch7:55–81), the corridor (ch7:121–129), then the first pole (ch7:225–227). A thirteen-year-old can follow the chain because each abstraction gets a person, object or door.
+- Count locks so far: non-protected record says renewals without inflating them (ch6:69); protected first pole alone says “renewed four times” (ch7:225). Lane bill introduced at ten counts, clean at eleven (ch4:191–215). Shadow’s rent and seal remain private to Cael/Lira/Brom/Karis; Seln is explicitly ignorant (ch4:237–245).
