editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-44.md:35:Nothing in it had changed. He had half thought something would, after the recess, after Ostrand and the borrowed office four streets back, as he had half thought the hill would look different on the morning after the case. But the wool exchange smelled of lanolin and damp coats, as it always had, and the forty benches ran back to the doors, a quarter full, with lot seventeen cut into the floor under his left boot. On the platform the hood sat in its place behind the long table, grey and still, and below it the five chairs of the evaluation seat stood in their row with their covers off and five people in them. Four were district evaluators whose names he had heard read once and had written down; and in the middle, with a file open on her knee at its usual angle, sat Ilsev.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:97:"Is borrowed." Seln very nearly smiled. "A records administrator's, on the third floor of a leasehold building four streets back from the registry seat. He is on circuit in the hill stations for six weeks. His landlord's keeper lends the room by the morning or the afternoon to anybody with a reason and a deposit, and writes the reason in a book, and does not read it twice. My reason is a reading." He looked at the note. "I have used that kind of room before, but never that one."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:115:It was a records administrator's room on the third floor of a leasehold building four streets back from the registry seat, with nothing of anyone's in it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-40.md:197:"I knew the system was imperfect. I didn't know it was designed to be."

