+### Movement 8 — chapters 48–54
+
+- The close fulfills the book’s argument at full scale. Ch48–49 first establishes a room of honest actors with no villain to expose (ch48:21–31), then gives Karis fifty-one minutes to prove the proposed discretion unwise without pretending that wisdom controls it (ch49:63–187). The ruling’s “lawful / compliant / nonetheless / revoked” paragraph makes the institutional hand visible precisely because every component person has acted honestly (ch51:173–201; ch51:243–263).
+- Calendar is exact against the ratified finish: Brom’s panel and the ruling share the last Fifth-day, day 201 (ch51:127–181); the council follows that night and the public bout the Sixth-day, day 202 (ch52:259–343; ch53:191–217; ch54:3–312). Withrow’s concealed notice arithmetic sets the evaluation for the last day of the year, day 207, turning the apparent five-week outer bound into five days (ch53:21–41, 97–129).
+- **Definite office-title continuity error:** ch49:201 has the clerk read “Evaluation-protocol certification: declined by the evaluator of record.” Gault is the evaluator of record throughout this book, including ch49:209; the Archmarshal’s office is the certifying office and supplied the refusal (ch46:253–295). Karis correctly calls it the certifying office at ch50:119–127. This should be the certifying office, provided the phrase is not protected.
+- Address continuity holds through the final ruling: *Caelen Hesk-ward* at ch48:35, ch49:43 and ch51:173. The ruling correctly uses the demonstration provision, standard Arbiter protocol and chapter fourteen consequences (ch51:177–195).
+- Knowledge boundaries hold. Ilsev reads the two returns and her “authorizing office: not traced” note without inferring the reserved maker or mechanism (ch50:241–291). Havel recognizes that the registry itself has now answered his oldest sheet but does not add the facts or infer beyond his chair (ch51:21–55, 81–121). The cache is argued as new matter but rejected because every verification route runs through the compromised instrument; no reserved truth below the case is spent (ch52:61–107).
+- The council earns its unusual length. It prices frame, fight and leaving at full strength, lets Karis advocate the losing route honestly, then makes each of five people state a different concrete cost (ch52:13–109, 113–253). Brom’s honest Iron finding coupled to the “regularize such associations” guidance is the most effective single demonstration of the system’s reach (ch52:127–177); his answer, three boxes, converts loyalty into work rather than speech.
+- The final bout earns two chapters. Exchange one exposes how the managed band has become involuntary waiting (ch53:249–299); exchange two spends the known ten-count lane bill cleanly (ch53:319–357); exchanges three and four demonstrate Blade’s edge/line without using the new acquisition, then produce the ninth fragment and a genuinely unpriced shoulder injury (ch54:3–158). It is spectacle, character settlement, capability audit and ethical test at once.
+- Capability/count locks hold. Two lanes cost ten counts each (ch54:270–278); Anchor repeatedly offers and remains unused (ch54:272–278); Shadow has nothing to offer before twelve hundred observers and remains sealed (ch54:270–273). Blade is the ninth confirmed fragment, while the anomaly remains outside the count (ch54:145–162, 262–278). Hesk’s clock continues losing (ch48:139–143; ch53:97–100, 159).
+- Brom’s day-45 envelope stays sealed on his table through the decision (ch50:19–23; ch53:119–121). He chooses not to read it and does not convert that choice into a claimed refusal.
+- Reader Standard holds. The densest legal close is organized around a list, a tool handle, a scale and two instruments; the thirteen-year-old reader never has to retain an unexplained abstract distinction. The shoulder dislocation is painful but not lurid or unsuitable.
+- Fullness is earned in ch48–49, ch52 and ch53–54. The one area that reads padded is the cumulative post-bout dispersal in ch54:164–312: Gault’s nod, multiple crowd reactions, Withrow leaving last, the Current girl, Ephram’s handshake, the full Log, the new-fragment threshold, Bracken’s four forms and the “Good room” retrospective each land separately, but together produce several successive emotional endings after the bout is already complete.
+- Texture watch reaches saturation: hands flat on tables, paper/objects squared to edges, quarter-turned rules/cups, prolonged silence, a character looking for a long moment, and “as a man/person does” explanatory similes recur in nearly every chapter here. The stronger repeated motifs (Hesk’s clock, Brom’s pocket/table, Seln’s cup, Bracken’s squares) need protection; generic uses around them need counting and reduction.
+
+### Movement 9 — chapters 55–60
+
+- Calendar and exit seam hold exactly. The four withdrawal leaves are signed on the Seventh-day, day 203, and the group leaves the hill at dusk (ch55:3–103; ch56:307–341). Seln is absent and meets them at the eighteenth stone on the First-day, day 204 (ch57:3–39; ch57:177–227; ch58:113–231). They leave the final waystation on the Fourth-day, day 207, the last day of the academic year (ch59:105–125), sleep at the last station, cross the Line the next morning (ch59:231–305), camp without fire under the cart, and reach the shelf on the following Sixth-day (ch59:351–395; ch60:191–203). Thus the shelf is the second camp past the Line and the first fire there (ch60:35–57), matching OWNER #46 and Book 7’s corrected entry.
+- The withdrawal mechanics pay the “clean door” lock: four enrollee files close *Withdrawn. Resigned in good standing* before the district officer serves the day-207 date (ch55:65–103; ch56:211–227). Withrow’s folder is clean, while Seln leaves outside the form and the watch report initially counts only three others (ch56:257–281; ch57:43–89). The first paper to count all five occurs at the provincial bound (ch59:131–149).
+- Counts and offices hold. Cael’s withdrawal form states two renewals (ch55:69–75), while the protected recalled first pole alone retains “a stamp renewed four times” (ch60:255–265). Gault’s final note correctly names himself evaluator of record (ch55:183–199). The Archmarshal summary correctly identifies his office as the certifying office (ch58:59–69), reinforcing that ch49:201 is the lone title error.
+- The day-45 Velmere envelope remains unbroken and is left, unopened, on Brom’s table beside the unsigned finding (ch56:145–161). His choice is stated as declining the particulars, not pretending the letter was answered.
+- Fragment continuity holds through the close. Blade is the ninth confirmed; the closing inventory names all nine, leaves Anchor’s source/name blank, and keeps session nine/Tide-adjacent separate as one anomaly (ch60:203–243). Shadow stays sealed beyond the Line even when the literal visibility condition is nearly exhausted, because Cael declines to test it on the first unwatched night (ch59:351–359); the inventory correctly says Seln knows why and the seal remains (ch60:205–219).
+- Kindling/reserved-truth boundaries hold. The abandoned station supplies an unfinished open register line, an older sigil stone around which the house was built, and a frame that correctly went quiet for Cael (ch59:187–229, 265–275), but no maker, age, Architect, Quieting or Tide practitioner is named. The maintenance slip at the file’s foot repeats institutional behavior without identifying the reserved hand behind it (ch60:289–321).
+- Hesk’s clock continues to lose through packing and the Line, then becomes the only clock available and is therefore “right” by local definition (ch55:237–243; ch59:333–347). This is a clean thematic conversion, not a continuity change.
+- Fuller M9 generally earns its length. Each departure is individuated by the thing the character is leaving: Lira’s own words on the form and Rooke’s *Hers* (ch55:13–37; ch56:43–91), Brom’s unsigned Iron / sealed family letter and three carried boxes (ch55:39–61; ch56:131–165, 185–253), Karis’s lapsed heads and surviving field archive (ch55:107–163; ch60:117–163), Seln’s correct empty record and first prepared fire (ch57:43–227), Cael’s file/room/Line inventory (ch55:237–255; ch60:191–275). These are different costs, not generic farewells.
+- The principal padding risk is ch56:1–341: after the four-leaf climax, Lira’s seminar, Rooke memory, Seln’s counter exit, Brom’s packing, box procession, district officer, Ephram, Withrow, Rooke, watchers, ferry and guesting-house Log all create a very long chain of exits. Nearly every beat is good; the accumulation delays road momentum and could lose two or three small explanatory callbacks without sacrificing any protected or packet-required event.
+- Road logistics are unusually strong and Reader-Standard clear: weights, box access, horse fatigue, water depth, the cart bed, chocks, fords and hand-carrying all follow observable physical rules (ch58:305–355; ch59:27–51, 447–493; ch60:3–53). The institutional taper is equally legible through disappearing metalling, milestones, hooks, boards, stamps and finally the churned turning ring (ch59:3–101, 125–163, 279–305).
+- The book’s paired argument closes without falsely cancelling its first half: “I can work within the system” remains true, and is set beside “The system was never designed to include me” (ch60:255–275). The final file escalation proves that leaving jurisdiction does not destroy the external machine, while the last line confines self-definition to Cael without claiming safety (ch60:289–371).
+- No content is unsuitable for thirteen. The long procedural aftermath is comprehensible because every status is attached to a physical leaf, room, road or drawer.
+- Definite defect count remains one: ch49:201’s office title. No new cross-movement continuity or knowledge-boundary defect found in M9.

