editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-56.md:67:It was her page. Her name stood at its head in his square capitals, and under it the figures, the trial and the hall's seal and the oak, each with its date. Below the figures were the two words he had written and never shown her; she had spent a term guessing at them, and had guessed kinder words than these.
