editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-52.md:63:"We have the thing that ends it," said Karis. "It's between Seln's feet. I spent fifty-one minutes last week telling a seat that its instrument had failed to read him, and I couldn't say why. I know why. I can date it to within a renewal of a charter. That isn't an argument from discretion; it's the newest matter anybody has put before the registry in two hundred years, and the code gives an appeal from a seat's ruling upon new matter. I looked it up on the night we came home from the close, because I couldn't sleep. It goes to the convening, within thirty days."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-52.md:87:"Then I'm found in a week," said Seln. "That is not a complaint, only the arithmetic. There is one leaf in that case that is not a copy. Somebody will ask who could have stood in a district's top-floor records room for five weeks, twelve years ago, and the service keeps its posting rolls very well. They would have me by the Seventh-day, and they would ask me what else I kept." He looked at the satchel between his feet. "After that it is no longer forty children and a leaf two hundred years old. It is an officer of the monitoring service who stole from a press, and the broadsides would print that instead. It is a better story, and it is also true."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-49.md:143:And it could not be said, in this room or in any room that stood on it. She had worked that out herself, over five nights, and had been the one to tell them. So she turned it face down. She did it where she stood, in front of two hundred people, with her thumb, and nobody saw.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-50.md:223:Cael had not known how large it was. He had seen it with thirty people in it and with two hundred, and never as it stood now, with the forty benches running back bare to the doors and the lot numbers showing in the floor between them. The high east windows laid four long bars of light across the boards. There was nobody on the steps outside, for nobody had been told. A return was posted in the porch after it was made.

