editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-59.md:77:*By charter of the registry, this house being chartered: TIER VERIFICATION available at the district station, Ostrand, four days west. No station lies east of the river crossing, and the station at the ford is unstaffed. TRAVEL ENDORSEMENTS may be lodged at this house for forward transmission; allow twenty days. ENROLLMENT INQUIRIES by the same. The chartered rates of this house are posted within. Complaints of a chartered house lie to the district seat.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-59.md:377:*The rematch stands. Not postponed — relocated. It happens on a floor nobody owns, and I think you'd prefer that anyway; a Gold-tier fact and an unclassified one, fighting where no seal can score either of us, is the only honest version of the bout, and we both knew it at Norhold. Find me when you're ready to fight something no ladder built. I'll be east.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-54.md:264:*Nine. Taken in earnest from a friend who asked me to show him straight — so I showed him straight, and the architecture did what it does with earnest, and the notice said "non-hostile," which it has never said, because there has never been a fight like it in the log. Ephram asked for the true measurement. He got it. He doesn't know he gave me a piece of himself for it; he consented to a fight, not to the thing the fight fed. I wrote the price down before the bout, the way the covenant says, so that when it cost — and it cost — I'd have written the cost before I collected it, which is the only line between me and what the office did at a road cut and in a records hall — spending people whose names it never bothered to write down, and asking nobody anything.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-29.md:73:*What you carry is worth what it has not done.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-51.md:177:"*The seat, having heard the petition and the responses in full, and having found the enrollment lawful in its execution and the respondent institution compliant with its charter throughout — which findings stand undisturbed — nonetheless finds the evaluation-integrity question sustained on the merits. The demonstration provision describes the practitioner; it does not evaluate him within the meaning of the integrity provisions. The petition for compelled re-evaluation under standard Arbiter protocol is granted. The re-evaluation shall be conducted at the district Arbiter station within five weeks. Should the re-evaluation return no valid classification, the procedure of the code's chapter fourteen shall apply: nullification, suspension, asset-restriction. The demonstration-provision enrollment is revoked effective at the close of the present academic year.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-57.md:47:*Teaching assistant, Bronze grade, fifteen years' service, absent without notice from first bell of the First-day. Residence room found vacated; no personal effects; bed made. All working files completed and cross-indexed to date. Inner-door key, records-press key, post-room key and wing side-door key surrendered on the copying-table blotter. Floor schedule posted one week forward. No note left, no leave applied for, no address of forwarding held by this house. The house records no disciplinary matter, no irregularity of any kind in the two years of this posting, and no view as to cause. Query submitted to the placing district office per code; direction requested.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-06-the-compacts-hand/manuscript/chapter-32.md:116:*Eight. Taken from someone the system sent namelessly, to hold me namelessly. No paper. No seal. No office to write to, not even a false one this time. She stood in the road and did the best thing she knew how to do, and I took it off her, and she'll go home tonight to wherever they keep her and nobody will ask her how her day was. A hand and no face. I don't know what I owe someone I can't find. I don't know if owing is the word. Write it down anyway.*

