+## 7. Rhythm outliers
+
+Whole-book meter: 296,518 words; 21,766 sentences; sentence mean 13.62, median 10; 28.5% at five words or fewer; 4.0% at forty or more; paragraph mean 38.95, median 27; 254 marked scene breaks; 944 words per scene; Flesch reading ease 89.1; FK grade 4.21. The scene figure is almost exactly the 950-word working target. The book is syntactically easier than the formula proxy, which suits the Reader Standard.
+
+- **Ch57 is the clearest long-metre outlier:** 5,089 words; sentence mean 16.69, median 15; paragraph mean 46.69, median 45. The extended Seln retrospective and report-voice make the long paragraphs purposeful (ch57:43–89, :95–157, :203–227), but this is the one chapter where the book's pulse visibly changes.
+- **Ch14 is the second long-metre outlier:** 3,504 words; sentence mean 16.53, median 12.5; paragraph mean 50.78, median 38; 6.1% of sentences at forty words or more. Vastin's inward, institutional reading justifies the slower syntax (ch14:45–148). No meter-only cut is needed.
+- **Ch22, ch26 and ch30** also run longer than the norm at means 15.69, 15.21 and 15.62; ch26 has 6.7% of sentences at forty-plus words. They are council, sitting and road-setup chapters, and remain readable (ch22:41–63, :91–149; ch26:65–115, :193–221; ch30:13–87, :171–239).
+- **Ch33, ch52 and ch59 are clipped outliers:** means/medians 12.12/7, 12.20/9 and 12.43/8.5. Ch33's recovery experiments, ch52's five-person council, and ch59's road inventory use lists and dialogue, so the clip is functional (ch33:25–215; ch52:13–171; ch59:3–163, :231–395).
+- **Length alone:** ch59 is longest at 7,980 words and ch53 next at 7,440. Both have seven effective scene units and roughly 1,000 words per scene; neither is a structural outlier. Ch56 feels longer than its measure because it chains exits rather than because its sentence meter departs.
+
+Verdict on rhythm: no chapter requires a meter repair. The texture pass should address repeated staging, not force every chapter toward the mean.
